# Test: OH radical PUMP2 single-point energy / 6-31G(d,p)
# Open-shell doublet (5 alpha / 4 beta electrons).
#
# Reference (Gaussian g09, frozen_core=auto):
#   UMP2  energy : -75.5320851 Ha
#   <S^2> (UMP2) :  0.7552
#   PUMP2 energy : -75.5335707 Ha
#   <S^2>_A      :  0.7500
#   PUMP2 correction = -1.4856 mHa
#
# Current StudDFT formula = (2/K_eff)*X_cross (Schlegel 1986 Hylleraas form,
# cross-doubles only).  This system has very small spin contamination
# (Delta<S^2> = 0.0052), so the cross-doubles term dominates and the
# residual against g09 PMP2-0 is ~3e-5 Ha.  See PUMP2_FORMULA.md for the
# discussion of higher-order singles/same-spin contributions that are
# not yet implemented.
#
# StudDFT v0.63.x output (cross-doubles only):
#   PUMP2 correction = -1.5120 mHa     (residual: -2.6e-5 Ha vs g09)
#
%method  MP2
%basis   6-31G(d,p)
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    2
%spin    unrestricted
%pump2   yes
%frozen_core 1

*geometry angstrom
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   0.969000
*end
